From: FlipperEmu
Subject: [PATCH] hw/timer/armv7m_systick: ignore updates of the unselected clock

systick_cpuclk_update() and systick_refclk_update() test whether the
updated clock is the one SYST_CSR.CLKSOURCE selects, and the comments say
the update can then be ignored, but the early return is missing. A board
that changes HCLK at runtime (and with it refclk = HCLK/8) therefore
re-times SysTick from refclk even though the guest selected the CPU clock.

Seen with the STM32WB55 Flipper Zero model: after the switch from MSI to
the 64 MHz PLL the 1 ms tick (LOAD=63999, CLKSOURCE=1) fired every 8 ms.

Signed-off-by: FlipperEmu
---
--- a/hw/timer/armv7m_systick.c
+++ b/hw/timer/armv7m_systick.c
@@ -220,6 +220,7 @@
 
     if (!(s->control & SYSTICK_CLKSOURCE)) {
         /* currently using refclk, we can ignore cpuclk changes */
+        return;
     }
 
     ptimer_transaction_begin(s->ptimer);
@@ -233,6 +234,7 @@
 
     if (s->control & SYSTICK_CLKSOURCE) {
         /* currently using cpuclk, we can ignore refclk changes */
+        return;
     }
 
     ptimer_transaction_begin(s->ptimer);
